// Hand-curated skills and their per-rules-set categories (skills,
// skill_rules_sets).
//
// Two sections, kept in one file so a skill's existence and its category can
// be reviewed against the same source page side by side:
//
//   skills         -- only skills no source importer can ever create, i.e.
//                     skills that exist solely in CRP, CRP+ or BB2016. A
//                     skill BBL or TP also knows needs no entry: its own
//                     upsert registers the same "Name" external id this file
//                     would, so both land on one row.
//   skillRulesSets -- the category table for EVERY skill, whichever importer
//                     introduces it. A missing row means "this rules set does
//                     not have this skill", and the BBL/TP skills imports read
//                     these rows back before recording a starting skill: an
//                     uncurated (skill, rules set) pair is reported as an
//                     import error naming this file.
//
// Every id in both sections is the skill's own display name, which is what
// NameExternalIdService.forSkill produces and what both source importers send.
// A skill whose display name carries a parenthetical value ("Loner (4+)",
// "Mighty Blow (+1)") is a DISTINCT skill here, because that is how both
// sources spell it: BBL prints it in one cell, and TP composes it from the
// skill's name plus its skillAttributeMaster value.
//
// 'unique' is a category like any other: it is the only marker a star
// player's exclusive skill has -- there is no per-association flag. This
// file curates no 'unique' rows: CRP's own "SKILL CATEGORIES" table (p.21)
// has no Extraordinary-vs-unique split, and cross-checking the CRP Star
// Players list (pp.79-80) found no skill there that is not already one of
// the 75 skills the categories table itself lists (i.e. no star-player-only
// skill to mark unique). Every CRP-era Extraordinary skill is curated as
// 'trait' per the task's mapping instructions.
//
// Sources, this file:
//   CRP -- m750496a_BB_Competition_Rules_Pack.pdf:
//          - p.21, "SKILL CATEGORIES" table -- the category for every skill.
//          - pp.19-21, "SKILL DESCRIPTIONS" -- each skill's own heading
//            confirms its category and exact spelling; used to cross-check
//            the categories table and to resolve the one "Claw / Claws"
//            combined table entry into the two literal spellings CRP's own
//            team rosters actually use (see the Mutation group below).
//          - pp.22-25, "TEAM ROSTERS" -- the 21 core CRP races' starting
//            skills, cross-checked against the categories table; introduced
//            no skill the table did not already list.
//   CRP -- Stunty_Leeg_Handbook_v1_0.pdf, "STUNTY TEAM ROSTERS" (pp.7-16) and
//          "STAR PLAYERS" (pp.17+) -- the 15 Stunty Leeg races and their star
//          players, checked for any skill not already in the CRP categories
//          table. None found: every skill name on these rosters (allowing for
//          this handbook's own inconsistent "Claw"/"Claws" and
//          "Side Step"/"Sidestep" spellings, and a "Regenerate" typo for
//          "Regeneration") already appears in the CRP core book's list, so
//          this file adds no Stunty-Leeg-only `skills` entries.
//
// (CRP+ and BB2016 sources are out of scope for this file -- see a later
// curation task/file for those rules sets' category rows.)
//
// `skills` entries below were identified by diffing the 76 skill spellings
// this file curates for CRP against every literal skillMaster/skills-cell
// string actually present in the downloaded tools/import-bbl and
// tools/import-tp data dumps (the modern-era source data BBL/TP's own
// upserts read). Three CRP-table skills never appear in either dump under
// any spelling and are curated below. A fourth near-miss, "Blood Lust", is
// curated too: TP's data only ever spells it "Bloodlust" (one word), so an
// entry under CRP's own two-word spelling is still needed for this file's
// (skill, CRP) rows to resolve -- flagged below rather than silently
// resolved, since only the developer can confirm whether these should be
// treated as the same skill or kept distinct.
{
  externalSystems: [
    { name: 'Name', category: 'bookkeeping' },
  ],
  skills: [
    // --- CRP-only skills: absent from every downloaded BBL/TP roster, match
    // or skillMaster record under any spelling (checked pp.19-21) ---
    { name: "Nurgle's Rot", externalIds: [{ system: 'Name', id: "Nurgle's Rot" }] },
    { name: 'Stakes', externalIds: [{ system: 'Name', id: 'Stakes' }] },
    // TODO: verify -- TP's downloaded data only ever spells this skill
    // "Bloodlust" (one word); BBL's downloaded data has neither spelling.
    // Curated here under CRP's own two-word "Blood Lust" so this file's CRP
    // row for it resolves; confirm with the developer whether "Blood Lust"
    // and "Bloodlust" should instead be treated as the same skill (which
    // would need TP's importer to normalize the spelling, not a curated
    // second skill row).
    { name: 'Blood Lust', externalIds: [{ system: 'Name', id: 'Blood Lust' }] },
  ],
  skillRulesSets: [
    // --- CRP: General skills (CRP p.21) ---
    { skill: { system: 'Name', id: 'Block' }, rulesSet: { system: 'Name', id: 'CRP' }, category: 'general' },
    { skill: { system: 'Name', id: 'Pass Block' }, rulesSet: { system: 'Name', id: 'CRP' }, category: 'general' },
    { skill: { system: 'Name', id: 'Dauntless' }, rulesSet: { system: 'Name', id: 'CRP' }, category: 'general' },
    { skill: { system: 'Name', id: 'Pro' }, rulesSet: { system: 'Name', id: 'CRP' }, category: 'general' },
    { skill: { system: 'Name', id: 'Dirty Player' }, rulesSet: { system: 'Name', id: 'CRP' }, category: 'general' },
    { skill: { system: 'Name', id: 'Shadowing' }, rulesSet: { system: 'Name', id: 'CRP' }, category: 'general' },
    { skill: { system: 'Name', id: 'Fend' }, rulesSet: { system: 'Name', id: 'CRP' }, category: 'general' },
    { skill: { system: 'Name', id: 'Strip Ball' }, rulesSet: { system: 'Name', id: 'CRP' }, category: 'general' },
    { skill: { system: 'Name', id: 'Frenzy' }, rulesSet: { system: 'Name', id: 'CRP' }, category: 'general' },
    { skill: { system: 'Name', id: 'Sure Hands' }, rulesSet: { system: 'Name', id: 'CRP' }, category: 'general' },
    { skill: { system: 'Name', id: 'Kick' }, rulesSet: { system: 'Name', id: 'CRP' }, category: 'general' },
    { skill: { system: 'Name', id: 'Tackle' }, rulesSet: { system: 'Name', id: 'CRP' }, category: 'general' },
    // TODO: verify -- BBL's downloaded data only ever spells this
    // "Kick-off Return" (lowercase "off"); CRP's own heading (p.20) and
    // categories table (p.21) both spell it "Kick-Off Return". Curated here
    // under CRP's own spelling; confirm whether BBL's importer should
    // normalize the case instead of this staying a second skill row.
    { skill: { system: 'Name', id: 'Kick-Off Return' }, rulesSet: { system: 'Name', id: 'CRP' }, category: 'general' },
    { skill: { system: 'Name', id: 'Wrestle' }, rulesSet: { system: 'Name', id: 'CRP' }, category: 'general' },

    // --- CRP: Agility skills (CRP p.21) ---
    { skill: { system: 'Name', id: 'Catch' }, rulesSet: { system: 'Name', id: 'CRP' }, category: 'agility' },
